{
  "title": "make ai-eval aborts the whole suite on one transient provider error",
  "description": "in_batches (cli/src/ai_eval/mod.rs) treats any AiError that isn't a validation failure as fatal (`Err(e) => return Err(e.into())`), so one transient upstream error aborts the whole `make ai-eval` run and nothing is written. \
Seen while regenerating photo-extraction for PR fixing photo nutrition: a 60 s request timeout from deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash, and `Provider error (code 403): Output blocked by content filtering policy` from anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 on an ordinary cookbook page. \
Each run took several retries. \
Because rejected (invalid) answers aren't cached, every rerun re-asks them, so the rows of models with invalid answers (gemini-2.5-flash, deepseek-v4.1-flash) also shift between otherwise cached reruns. \
Consider retrying transport errors and timeouts a few times before giving up, then counting a persistent provider refusal for one case as invalid (with its message under Rejected answers) instead of aborting.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "ai",
  ],
